2026-11-07T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2481) 'Slow commits and server-side evidence
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2481  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2481) 'On a 4-process scratch cluster, three repeats, 15 s cells: slow commits over 100 ms clustered 24 times across the 12 cells, 14 touching more than one process and 10 touching one (8 at N=1, 2 at N=8). A lone writer stalled in 2 of 3 repeats (5 and 4 commits over 100 ms), so sharing alone does not explain the stalls. Server CPU stayed near half a core, Ratekeeper said limited_by=workload throughout, and scratch trace logs held one SlowTask event in total and no disk-stall events. The scratch tlog shares the Mac's SSD with the production cluster; that is an untested candidate.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2481  1 LINE
 Text:Written
